    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "JDG16:4",
        "textualBasisJa": "It came to pass afterward that he loved a woman in the valley of Sorek, whose name was Delilah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG16:6",
        "textualBasisJa": "Delilah said to Samson, “Please tell me where your great strength lies, and what you might be bound to afflict you.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG16:10",
        "textualBasisJa": "Delilah said to Samson, “Behold, you have mocked me, and told me lies. Now please tell me how you might be bound.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG16:12",
        "textualBasisJa": "So Delilah took new ropes and bound him with them, then said to him, “The Philistines are on you, Samson!” The ambush was waiting in the inner room. He broke them off his arms like a thread."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG16:13",
        "textualBasisJa": "Delilah said to Samson, “Until now, you have mocked me and told me lies. Tell me with what you might be bound.” He said to her, “If you weave the seven locks of my head with the fabric on the loom.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG16:18",
        "textualBasisJa": "When Delilah saw that he had told her all his heart, she sent and called for the lords of the Philistines, saying, “Come up this once, for he has told me all his heart.” Then the lords of the Philistines came up to her and brought the money in their hand."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JDG16:19",
        "textualBasisJa": "She made him sleep on her knees; and she called for a man, and shaved off the seven locks of his head; and she began to torment him, and his strength went from him."
      }
    ],
